## Overview

Create React Email templates for commerce transactional emails and add typed methods to the existing `emailService` singleton. The platform already uses Resend + partner SMTP via `lib/email/service.ts` — this ticket adds commerce-specific templates and wiring only. No new email infrastructure needed.

## Architecture

### Email Service Pattern

The existing `EmailService` class in `lib/email/service.ts` (line 95) follows a consistent pattern for every email type:

1. **Props type** exported from the template file (e.g., `OrganizationInvitationEmailProps`)
2. **Template component** as a named export React function (e.g., `OrganizationInvitationEmail()`)
3. **Typed method** on `emailService` that:
   * Dynamic-imports the template
   * Calls the component with props to get a React element
   * Renders to HTML via `render(component)` and plaintext via `render(component, { plainText: true })`
   * Sends via `this.sendEmailOrThrow(payload, partnerConfig)`

Reference implementation: `sendOrganizationInvitationEmail()` at line 325 of `lib/email/service.ts`.

### Templates to Create

All templates go in `lib/email/templates/` and follow the exact React Email component pattern from `lib/email/templates/organization-invitation-email.tsx`:

* Imports: `Body, Button, Container, Head, Heading, Hr, Html, Link, Preview, Section, Text` from `<mention>/components`, `Tailwind` from `<mention>/tailwind`
* Wrapper: `<Html><Head/><Preview>...</Preview><Tailwind><Body>...<Container>...</Container></Body></Tailwind></Html>`
* Store branding (logo, colors, store name) applied to all templates via props

---

#### 1\. `order-confirmation-email.tsx`

**Props:**

```typescript
export type OrderConfirmationEmailProps = {
  storeName: string;
  storeLogo?: string;
  orderNumber: string;
  orderDate: string;
  items: Array<{
    name: string;
    quantity: number;
    unitPrice: string; // pre-formatted
    imageUrl?: string;
  }>;
  subtotal: string;
  shippingTotal: string;
  taxTotal: string;
  total: string;
  shippingAddress: {
    name: string;
    line1: string;
    line2?: string;
    city: string;
    state: string;
    postalCode: string;
    country: string;
  };
  guestTrackingUrl?: string; // only for guest orders (uses lookupToken)
  orderHistoryUrl?: string;  // only for authenticated users
};
```

**emailService method:**

```typescript
public async sendOrderConfirmationEmail(
  input: OrderConfirmationEmailProps & {
    recipient: string;
    partnerConfig?: CachedPartnerConfig | null;
  }
): Promise<void> {
  const { OrderConfirmationEmail } = await import(
    './templates/order-confirmation-email'
  );
  const component = OrderConfirmationEmail(input);
  const html = await render(component);
  const text = await render(component, { plainText: true });

  await this.sendEmailOrThrow(
    {
      recipient: input.recipient,
      subject: `Order #${input.orderNumber} confirmed`,
      html,
      text,
    },
    input.partnerConfig || null
  );
}
```

